Detailed Breakdown in Simple Words:
• 1. Response Speed: When you send a prompt, the AI usually takes time to read it (cold start). By reusing saved prompt memory
(cache hit), ThermaCache cuts wait times by over 68%. Rebuilding the router in C++ will make this almost instantaneous.
• 2. User Capacity: In our first test, we sent requests one by one to prove the logic works. Next, we will upgrade the code so 128
people can send requests at the exact same moment without memory locks or crashes.
• 3. Efficiency & Cost: Our test script was written in Python, which uses a lot of CPU power (96%). Rewriting it in C++ and Rust will
drop the CPU work to under 12%, making it very cheap for data centers to run.
• 4. Heat Control: When GPUs get too hot (over 80°C), NVIDIA automatically slows them down to protect the hardware.
ThermaCache keeps temperatures cool around 58°C–63°C, so the GPUs never overheat or slow down.
